<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ismail Kamil Pasha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1795–<a href="/years/1822">1822</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ismail Kamil Pasha was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-of-egypt">Muhammad Ali of Egypt</a>. In 1820 and 1821 he led the Egyptian army that defeated the Shaigiya and conquered the Funj Sultanate, beginning Turco-Egyptian rule in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>. In 1822 he was burned to death at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shendi">Shendi</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaalin">Ja'alin</a> ruler Mek Nimr, whom he had humiliated.</p></div>
